Date: Mon, 12 Apr 93 00:01:17 -0700
From: zz@garnet.berkeley.edu (Zachary Zaidman)
Subject: Libertarians accepting govt. $ ?

On accepting government $.

Hi everyone! I have been quite absent from this list for some 
time due to much work and little time. There is something I have 
been meaning to share with many of you since I have felt lonely in 
my efforts to think about it on my own. I think many of you are familiar 
(or friendly) with my own political convictions. I am posing this 
dilemma to _you_ as a way of inviting you to think through (and help 
me think through if you so desire) its most important issues. 

As many of you, I am a Libertarian who lives in a statist system and I 
have to do my best to integrate these two conditions without playing 
martyr and without loosing my integrity either.

I have a personal desire to be morally and logically consistent 
whenever possible, but in the case of accepting government money 
I am not sure how I feel. I know that if I give it up it will not go back to 
those who have _made_ it (and this is only the beginning of that argument). But I feel uneasy about playing a part in this system and 
benefiting from it even though I am often compelled to do so. I am 
sure many of you are familiar with this particular dilemma and may 
have thought about it more than I have.

Among other activities, I am working towards a graduate degree for 
which I have recently  been awarded a big federal fellowship. I am almost certain that I will accept the award and I think it would be 
irrational at this stage not to. However, I do not want to catch myself 
making justifications without having careful arguments to support my 
actions. I have more than a few reasons to believe that I am doing 
the "right thing" but I wonder what experiences others have had with 
this kind of thinking.

Replies to my personal email address are especially welcome and 
more likely to get my full attention, but I will also try _very_ hard to 
spend more time at least lurking on this list since I miss it (and you) 
quite a bit.

Cheers,
--zak

